.TH DAMX-SETUP 1 "2026-10-07" "DAMX 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
damx-setup \- post-install helper for Div Acer Manager Max
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B damx-setup
.RI [ option ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B damx-setup
inspects the DAMX installation and performs optional post-install steps that
require root privileges.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --status
Print the state of the daemon service, the Nitro/PredatorSense button service
and the Linuwu-Sense kernel drivers. This is the default when no option is
given.
.TP
.B --drivers
Clone (or update) the Linuwu-Sense driver sources, build them against the
running kernel and install the kernel modules. Requires kernel headers, a C
compiler and git. Secure Boot systems additionally require signed modules.
.TP
.B --nitro
Configure the Nitro/PredatorSense hardware button so it launches DAMX for the
current desktop user, and enable the
.I nitro-key-detection.service
unit. Requires the
.B evtest
package.
.TP
.B --disable-nitro
Disable and remove the Nitro button configuration.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DAMX_TARGET_USER
Desktop user that should be used for the Nitro button launcher instead of the
auto-detected user.
.TP
.B DAMX_DRIVER_REPO
Git URL used by
.B \-\-drivers
(default: the Div-Linuwu-Sense repository on GitHub).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR damx (1)
.SH AUTHOR
PXDiv and contributors.
